        textProvided: "3 Oct. 63<br>The Kilns,<br>Headington Quarry,<br>Oxford<br><br>Dear Mr. Meškys<br><br>By all means use the poem as far as I am concerned: but I expect you need <i>Punch’s</i> permission as well.<br><br>I fear Numinor (=Atlantis) is the only point at which there is a tie between Tolkien’s mythology and mine. When you’ll get any more in print from him, Lord knows. You see, he is both a procrastinator & a perfectionist. You have no idea with what laborious midwifery we got the <i>Lord of the Rings</i> out of him!<br><br>I’d write more if I were not rather ill. <br><br>Yours sincerely<br>C.S. Lewis",
