        textProvided: "The Kilns, Headington Quarry, Oxford<br>23/9/55<br><br>Dear Shephard [sic] (If we may drop the honorifics)<br><br>Thanks for yours of 17<sup>th.</sup> & enclosure. I’ve nothing to add to it except perhaps this; that references to other works shd. be workable for cheap texts as well as scholarly editions where both exist (e.g. reference to Malory shd. give Caxton’s Bk & cap. & Everyman vol. & p. as well as Vinaver). On p. 2. para. 5. perhaps for <i>In all other…chosen</i> read <i>so far as this limitation of length permits</i>, ? The text as it stands is a bit clumsy.<br><br>Yours<br>C.S. Lewis",
